statement.p:
Let N + be a directed phylogenetic network (respectively, N a semi-directed phylogenetic network), and let k be some non-negative integer. Then, we call the network N + (respectively, N)
level-k if there are at most k reticulation nodes in each blob of the network;
strict level-k if the network is level-k but not level-(k − 1);
stack-free if none of the reticulation nodes of the network are stacked;
simple if the network has a single non-leaf blob;
triangle-free if the network contains no cycles of length three, where edge directions are disregarded;
outer-labeled planar if the network has a planar embedding without crossing edges and with the leaves on the outside.
